From: Octagon SF8008 port
Subject: [PATCH] bcm: reset the display list when exec_list() cannot flush

exec_list() returns early when no framebuffer is open, without clearing
ptr. Callers such as dreambcm_bcm_ensure_space() and bcm_accel_blit()
call it precisely to make room in displaylist[] and then keep appending
through the P() macro, which does no bounds checking. On a machine
without the proprietary hifb accel ioctl this overflows the 1024 entry
array and corrupts adjacent static data, crashing enigma2 as soon as
fonts are rendered.

Drop the queued operations in that path so ptr stays within bounds.

Upstream-Status: Pending
--- a/lib/gdi/bcm.cpp
+++ b/lib/gdi/bcm.cpp
@@ -524,7 +524,16 @@
 		int len;
 	} l;
 
-	if (fb_fd < 0) return -1;
+	if (fb_fd < 0)
+	{
+		/* Nothing can be flushed without a framebuffer, but the queued
+		 * operations must still be dropped. Callers use exec_list() to
+		 * make room in displaylist[] and keep appending with P()
+		 * regardless of the return value, so leaving ptr untouched
+		 * overflows the array. */
+		ptr = 0;
+		return -1;
+	}
 
 	l.ptr = displaylist;
 	l.len = ptr;
